# Copy to `.env.local` and adjust for your environment.
#
# WARNING: every NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable is compiled into the JavaScript bundle
# shipped to every visitor's browser. It is not read at request time on a
# server — it is baked in at build time and readable by anyone who opens
# devtools. Nothing secret may ever go in a NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable. There is
# no backend secret (DATABASE_URL, REDIS_URL, SESSION_SECRET) that belongs
# here; those live only in the backend's own environment.

# The API's origin: scheme + host + port, no path, no trailing /api.
# frontend/src/lib/config.ts derives both the REST base (`{origin}/api`) and,
# by default, the WebSocket base from this single value — that is what keeps
# the two from silently drifting apart (e.g. HTTPS working while the socket
# still points at plain ws://).
#
# Local default (matches the backend's local port, 8001):
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8001
#
# Production example:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://syncboard-api.onrender.com

# Optional: overrides the WebSocket origin instead of deriving it from
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL above (http:// -> ws://, https:// -> wss://). Only
# needed if sockets terminate somewhere other than the API's own origin.
# Leave unset in the normal case.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL=wss://syncboard-api.onrender.com
